# Skilleraa — Coding Style

## Naming
- Components / pages: `PascalCase.jsx` (`StudentDashboard.jsx`)
- Libs / hooks / utils: `camelCase.js` (`jobsService.js`, `useX` if hooks added)
- SQL migrations: `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_snake_description.sql`
- Python modules: `snake_case.py`
- Env vars: `SCREAMING_SNAKE`; frontend must use `REACT_APP_` prefix
- Test ids: `data-testid="kebab-case"`

## React
- Function components only; colocate page logic with existing shells
- Data in `lib/*Service.js` — not inline Supabase in deep trees when a service exists
- Always handle loading, error (`ErrorState`), empty (`EmptyState`)
- Prefer existing `uiClasses` / patterns over new design systems
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`; no new `console.log` (use `lib/logger.js`)
- Avoid new `useMemo`/`useCallback` unless profiling shows need
- Do not duplicate components — extend `ConfirmModal`, `ErrorBoundary`, etc.

## FastAPI
- Validate with Pydantic; return clear HTTP errors
- Auth via Bearer JWT; check ownership/role before side effects
- Log method/path/status — never tokens or bodies
- Keep payments/uploads in dedicated modules
- `SEED_DEMO_DATA` must stay off in production

## SQL
- Additive migrations only; never drop prod tables/data casually
- Always RLS; prefer `security definer` + `set search_path = public` for helpers
- Qualify columns in policies (`payments.freelancer_id`, not bare names)
- Name policies descriptively: `"Clients can read own payments"`

## Tailwind
- Use existing tokens: `skl-border`, `font-display`, shared button classes
- Mobile-first; match spacing/radius used on sibling pages
- No purple-glow / generic AI theme drift; preserve current black/white Skilleraa look

## Component structure
```
pages/{role|public}/Feature.jsx  → shell + data + UI
components/                      → reusable UI
lib/                             → API/Supabase/helpers
context/                         → cross-cutting state (auth)
```
